  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "Combine mayonnaise, gochujang, yuzu, and chives in medium bowl and whisk to combine. Lay shrimp on paper towel-lined baking sheet and blot to fully dry.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "Heat peanut oil over high heat in a large, heavy dutch oven or wok to 390 degrees as read on an instant read or deep-frying thermometer, about 12 minutes. Lower heat to maintain temperature.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "primary_message": "Whisk flour and rice flour together in a large bowl. Add eggs and soda water and, shaking bowl with one hand, rapidly whisk with other hand with a pair of chopsticks until the mixture just comes together. There should still be dry clumps of flour remaining. Line a second bowl with a triple layer of paper towels.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "primary_message": "Working in two batches, submerge shrimp in batter and turn to coat. Pick up a handful of shrimp, allow excess batter to drip off, and carefully drop into hot oil one at a time. Repeat until first half of shrimp are all in the fryer. Fry, agitating constantly with chopsticks or wire mesh spider until tempura is a pale golden brown and very crisp, about 2 minutes. Transfer the fried shrimp to the paper-towel lined bowl, season with salt, and toss to drain excess oil. Transfer to a wire rack set in a rimmed baking sheet in a 200°F oven to keep warm. Allow oil to reheat to 390°F and repeat with remaining shrimp.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "primary_message": "Transfer drained shrimp to bowl with sauce and toss to coat. Serve immediately, sprinkled with extra chives.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
